RECENT CHANGES WORTH KNOWING
  Equipped gear now survives a quit. /std/weapon.c and /std/armour.c
  implement query_auto_load() gated on being wielded or worn, so worn
  and wielded items are captured into __AutoLoad before anything
  unequips. Loose inventory still drops on the floor on quit, exactly
  as before.
  Ranged combat has no separate command. The old shoot and fire
  commands were aliases for kill and have been removed. A wielded
  ranged weapon is fired by the normal combat round, which also spends
  one shot of ammo per attack.
  tell and reply are staff-contact only, and the intermud paths are
  staff-only too. Telepathy no longer seeds the tell reply buffer,
  because that had been handing players a free cross-room reply that
  skipped telepathy's ISP cost, introduction check, and mind block.
  Pets can be stored. stable puts one away as plain env strings on the
  owner; call brings it back.
  The chargen guide NPC is gone entirely. setter.c drives every prompt
  itself, and chargen answers are plain words with no verb prefix:
  americas, roll, reroll, human, scrupulous, headhunter, none.

